window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b315-c26d564f3c852f2b.json"]={sha256:"c26d564f3c852f2b0a9b281389f35ac57eabe75dfa0fe1fc5aaa46d3148fe3c0",value:{"id":"b315","title":"武漢—廣州高速鐵路","titleEn":"Wuhan–Guangzhou high-speed railway","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以武漢至廣州高速鐵路為背景，設計跨越濕熱平原和山地區段的教學走廊。課程將暴雨排水、隧道壓力和長坡牽引連結，要求在設備受潮、黏著下降與列車降速時重算能量、制動與班表影響。","summaryEn":"Use Wuhan–Guangzhou high-speed rail to construct a teaching corridor crossing humid plains and mountain sections. Connect storm drainage, tunnel pressure and sustained climbing. Recalculate energy, braking and timetable consequences when equipment becomes damp, adhesion falls and speed is restricted, retaining explicit boundaries between a hydraulic runoff estimate and a complete flood-protection design.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-highspeed","subcategoryTitle":"高速鐵路系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"High-speed rail systems","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-highspeed","learningTags":["rail","rail-highspeed","rail"],"architectureFamily":"rail-system","architectureNodes":[["路線與土建","Alignment and civil works"],["車輛與接觸","Vehicle and contact"],["牽引供電","Traction supply"],["行車控制","Movement control"],["車站與旅客","Stations and passengers"],["監測與維護","Monitoring and maintenance"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,1],[3,4],[4,5],[5,0],[5,3]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-system","labels":["路線與土建","車輛與接觸","牽引供電","行車控制","車站與旅客"],"labelsEn":["Alignment and civil works","Vehicle and contact","Traction supply","Movement control","Stations and passengers"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合原創算例：單元 1 得 flow=0.306 m^3/s；單元 2 得 travel=7.352941 s；單元 3 得 climbing=2354.4 kW。上述三個結果使用各單元明示的不同邊界，不能任意相加或視為實際工程實測值。以第一單元 rain 的擾動測試，結果改為 0.3366 m^3/s；學徒需先比較單位、敏感度和假設，再決定是否要細化模型。以武漢至廣州高速鐵路為背景，設計跨越濕熱平原和山地區段的教學走廊。課程將暴雨排水、隧道壓力和長坡牽引連結，要求在設備受潮、黏著下降與列車降速時重算能量、制動與班表影響。 最終交付應保留原始輸入、測點時間戳、誤差範圍與無法由簡化式證明的結論。","textEn":"Integrated original exercise: unit 1 gives flow=0.306 m^3/s; unit 2 gives travel=7.352941 s; unit 3 gives climbing=2354.4 kW. These three results use different explicit boundaries and must not be added or presented as measurements of the real railway. Perturbing rain in the first unit changes its result to 0.3366 m^3/s. Compare units, sensitivity and assumptions before deciding which model needs refinement. Use Wuhan–Guangzhou high-speed rail to construct a teaching corridor crossing humid plains and mountain sections. Connect storm drainage, tunnel pressure and sustained climbing. Recalculate energy, braking and timetable consequences when equipment becomes damp, adhesion falls and speed is restricted, retaining explicit boundaries between a hydraulic runoff estimate and a complete flood-protection design. The final submission should retain original inputs, measurement timestamps, uncertainty ranges and conclusions that the simplified expressions cannot establish.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b315-v16-s1","title":"集水與排水容量與隧道壓力波傳遞","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity & Tunnel pressure-wave travel","description":"本階段聚焦「集水與排水容量」與「隧道壓力波傳遞」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\" and \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b315-v16-01","title":"集水與排水容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「集水與排水容量」如何影響武漢—廣州高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wuhan–Guangzhou high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。鐵路集水範圍若只算軌道面，會漏掉坡面與站區流入。 合理化流量法假定雨強與集流條件相符，面積及逕流係數也須明確。它估算峰值流率而非完整洪水歷線；抽水或蓄水設計還需對時間積分和出口條件。 把山坡逕流與線路集水面積分開估算，檢查雨強時間尺度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「集水與排水容量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient. Actual drainage also depends on inlet blockage, pipe slope and downstream water level. Counting only track surface can omit inflow from adjacent slopes and station areas. The rational estimate assumes rainfall intensity compatible with catchment response and explicit area and runoff coefficient. It gives a peak rate, not a complete hydrograph. Pumping or storage design additionally requires time integration and outlet conditions. Estimate hillside runoff and railway catchment separately and check rainfall-intensity duration. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.306 m^3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.306 m^3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「集水與排水容量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-01-k1","title":"集水與排水容量","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity","text":"短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。鐵路集水範圍若只算軌道面，會漏掉坡面與站區流入。","textEn":"A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient. Actual drainage also depends on inlet blockage, pipe slope and downstream water level.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「集水與排水容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\" is correct?","options":["排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位","短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.","A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":1,"explanation":"短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b315-v16-02","title":"集水與排水容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「集水與排水容量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.306 m^3/s。敏感度：rain 單獨增加百分之十至 2.2e-05 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.3366 m^3/s。模型邊界：均勻降雨的合理化法概念；不含集流時間、水文頻率分析或蓄滯。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.306 m^3/s. Sensitivity: rain, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2.2e-05 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.3366 m^3/s. Model boundary: Uniform-rainfall rational-method concept; concentration time, frequency analysis and storage are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.306 m^3/s。敏感度：rain 單獨增加百分之十至 2.2e-05 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.3366 m^3/s。模型邊界：均勻降雨的合理化法概念；不含集流時間、水文頻率分析或蓄滯。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.306 m^3/s. Sensitivity: rain, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2.2e-05 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.3366 m^3/s. Model boundary: Uniform-rainfall rational-method concept; concentration time, frequency analysis and storage are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「集水與排水容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2。"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.306 m^3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.306 m^3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b315-v16-03","title":"集水與排水容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「集水與排水容量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。 核對雨量單位和有效集水邊界，量測泵浦出流與集水井水位變化，以體積守恆互證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater. Verify rainfall units and catchment boundaries, measure pump outflow and sump-level change, and cross-check them through volume conservation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將部分入口視為堵塞，建立地表暫存與排出的水量表；比較增加入口和增加泵量對不同瓶頸的效果。 再以本單元 rain 的對照值重算 flow，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Block selected inlets in the scenario, tabulate surface storage and discharge, and compare additional inlets with additional pumping for different bottlenecks. Also recalculate flow for the alternative rain value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。 核對雨量單位和有效集水邊界，量測泵浦出流與集水井水位變化，以體積守恆互證。","textEn":"Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater. Verify rainfall units and catchment boundaries, measure pump outflow and sump-level change, and cross-check them through volume conservation.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將部分入口視為堵塞，建立地表暫存與排出的水量表；比較增加入口和增加泵量對不同瓶頸的效果。 再以本單元 rain 的對照值重算 flow，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Block selected inlets in the scenario, tabulate surface storage and discharge, and compare additional inlets with additional pumping for different bottlenecks. Also recalculate flow for the alternative rain value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「集水與排水容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\"?","options":["現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好"],"optionsEn":["Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b315-v16-04","title":"集水與排水容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「集水與排水容量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 排水堵塞改變有效出流，不能只用較大泵浦銘牌值補償。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. Blocked drainage changes effective outflow and cannot be compensated merely by a larger pump nameplate rating. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把山坡逕流與線路集水面積分開估算，檢查雨強時間尺度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Estimate hillside runoff and railway catchment separately and check rainfall-intensity duration.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 排水堵塞改變有效出流，不能只用較大泵浦銘牌值補償。","textEn":"Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. Blocked drainage changes effective outflow and cannot be compensated merely by a larger pump nameplate rating.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「集水與排水容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":1,"explanation":"垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b315-v16-05","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「隧道壓力波傳遞」如何影響武漢—廣州高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wuhan–Guangzhou high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。入口緩衝設計影響波形上升率，波到達出口的時間與車身到達時間屬不同問題，須分開建立量測觸發。 波傳時間由傳播距離除以聲速決定，與列車走完整段的時間不同。此式只預測到達時序而不預測波幅；洞口形狀、列車頭型和反射決定的壓力變化須用其他流動模型。 在連續隧道與洞口測點之間比較聲波傳播時間和列車通過時間，另列波幅問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「隧道壓力波傳遞」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed. Entrance treatments affect the rise of the waveform. Wave arrival and train arrival are different events and require separate measurement triggers. Wave travel time is propagation distance divided by sound speed, not the time for the train to traverse the section. This expression predicts arrival timing, not amplitude. Portal geometry, train-nose shape and reflections require additional flow models to predict pressure changes. Compare acoustic travel time with train-passage time between tunnel and portal sensors, treating wave amplitude as a separate problem. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.352941 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.352941 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「隧道壓力波傳遞」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tunnel pressure-wave travel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-05-k1","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel","text":"列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。入口緩衝設計影響波形上升率，波到達出口的時間與車身到達時間屬不同問題，須分開建立量測觸發。","textEn":"A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed. Entrance treatments affect the rise of the waveform.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「隧道壓力波傳遞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\" is correct?","options":["隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動","列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。"],"optionsEn":["A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.","A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b315-v16-06","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：定量估算","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隧道壓力波傳遞」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.352941 s。敏感度：length 單獨增加百分之十至 2750 m，其餘固定，結果為 8.088235 s。模型邊界：一維線性聲學且音速均勻；不預測波幅、微壓波峰值或反射耗散。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.352941 s. Sensitivity: length, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2750 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 8.088235 s. Model boundary: One-dimensional linear acoustics with uniform sound speed; amplitude, micro-pressure-wave peaks and reflection losses are not predicted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.352941 s。敏感度：length 單獨增加百分之十至 2750 m，其餘固定，結果為 8.088235 s。模型邊界：一維線性聲學且音速均勻；不預測波幅、微壓波峰值或反射耗散。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.352941 s. Sensitivity: length, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2750 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 8.088235 s. Model boundary: One-dimensional linear acoustics with uniform sound speed; amplitude, micro-pressure-wave peaks and reflection losses are not predicted.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「隧道壓力波傳遞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s。","支承越柔軟所有頻率的振動就一定越小","煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","Softer supports necessarily reduce vibration at every frequency.","A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.352941 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.352941 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b315-v16-07","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隧道壓力波傳遞」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。 在洞口與洞內配置同步壓力測點，對照列車頭部通過時刻，分辨首波與後續反射。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately. Synchronise pressure sensors at the portal and inside the tunnel with nose-passage time, distinguishing the first wave from later reflections. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較壓力波與列車兩種到達時間，加入一次端部反射畫出事件圖，說明單一延遲量無法判斷出口微壓波是否超標。 再以本單元 length 的對照值重算 travel，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare wave and train arrival times, add one end reflection to the event diagram, and explain why travel time alone cannot establish compliance of portal micro-pressure waves. Also recalculate travel for the alternative length value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。 在洞口與洞內配置同步壓力測點，對照列車頭部通過時刻，分辨首波與後續反射。","textEn":"Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately. Synchronise pressure sensors at the portal and inside the tunnel with nose-passage time, distinguishing the first wave from later reflections.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較壓力波與列車兩種到達時間，加入一次端部反射畫出事件圖，說明單一延遲量無法判斷出口微壓波是否超標。 再以本單元 length 的對照值重算 travel，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare wave and train arrival times, add one end reflection to the event diagram, and explain why travel time alone cannot establish compliance of portal micro-pressure waves. Also recalculate travel for the alternative length value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「隧道壓力波傳遞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。","用平均電流代入平方損耗公式總能得到正確熱負荷"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately.","Squaring average current always gives the correct resistive heat load."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b315-v16-08","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隧道壓力波傳遞」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 單點峰值不足以判別首波，須檢查測點間傳遞時差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. A single peak cannot identify the first wave; inspect propagation delay between sensors. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在連續隧道與洞口測點之間比較聲波傳播時間和列車通過時間，另列波幅問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare acoustic travel time with train-passage time between tunnel and portal sensors, treating wave amplitude as a separate problem.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 單點峰值不足以判別首波，須檢查測點間傳遞時差。","textEn":"Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. A single peak cannot identify the first wave; inspect propagation delay between sensors.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「隧道壓力波傳遞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動","時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.","Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak."],"answer":2,"explanation":"時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b315-v16-s2","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率與黏著限制與可用牽引力","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power & Adhesion limit and usable traction","description":"本階段聚焦「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」與「黏著限制與可用牽引力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\" and \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b315-v16-09","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」如何影響武漢—廣州高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gradient resistance and climbing power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wuhan–Guangzhou high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車爬坡需提高重力位能，坡度小時沿線重力分量約等於重量乘坡度。功率還與速度相乘，因此相同牽引力下高速爬坡更耗功率；下坡則需處理持續制動能量而非僅一次停車。 坡度以升高量除以水平距離表示，百分比與小數不可混用。此項只表示重力位能增加的速率，總牽引功率還要加上加速、滾動、氣動及轉換損失。 對長坡計算持續重力功率，另列加速與空氣阻力需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Climbing raises gravitational potential energy. For small gradients, the along-track gravity force is approximately weight times gradient. Multiplication by speed gives power, making faster climbing more demanding at equal force; descending requires continuous energy management rather than merely one stopping event. Gradient is rise divided by horizontal distance, so percentage and decimal representations must not be mixed. This term only gives the rate of gravitational potential-energy increase. Total traction demand also includes acceleration, rolling resistance, aerodynamics and conversion losses. Calculate sustained gravitational power on a long climb and separately list acceleration and drag demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gradient resistance and climbing power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=300000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s；計算：climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2354.4 kW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=300000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s; calculation: climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2354.4 kW.","failure":"常見誤解：「長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gradient resistance and climbing power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-09-k1","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power","text":"列車爬坡需提高重力位能，坡度小時沿線重力分量約等於重量乘坡度。功率還與速度相乘，因此相同牽引力下高速爬坡更耗功率；下坡則需處理持續制動能量而非僅一次停車。","textEn":"Climbing raises gravitational potential energy. For small gradients, the along-track gravity force is approximately weight times gradient.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\" is correct?","options":["列車爬坡需提高重力位能，坡度小時沿線重力分量約等於重量乘坡度。","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動","電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著"],"optionsEn":["Climbing raises gravitational potential energy.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.","A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"列車爬坡需提高重力位能，坡度小時沿線重力分量約等於重量乘坡度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Climbing raises gravitational potential energy. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b315-v16-10","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率：定量估算","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gradient resistance and climbing power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=300000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s；計算：climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2354.4 kW。敏感度：mass 單獨增加百分之十至 330000 kg，其餘固定，結果為 2589.84 kW。模型邊界：小坡度且定速；不含空阻、輪阻、加速與傳動損失。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=300000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s; calculation: climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2354.4 kW. Sensitivity: mass, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 330000 kg, with all other inputs fixed, gives 2589.84 kW. Model boundary: Small gradient and constant speed; aerodynamic drag, rolling resistance, acceleration and drive losses are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=300000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s；計算：climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2354.4 kW。敏感度：mass 單獨增加百分之十至 330000 kg，其餘固定，結果為 2589.84 kW。模型邊界：小坡度且定速；不含空阻、輪阻、加速與傳動損失。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=300000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s; calculation: climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2354.4 kW. Sensitivity: mass, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 330000 kg, with all other inputs fixed, gives 2589.84 kW. Model boundary: Small gradient and constant speed; aerodynamic drag, rolling resistance, acceleration and drive losses are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\", which statement holds?","options":["速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=300000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s。","濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好"],"optionsEn":["A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.","Original hypothetical exercise.","Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=300000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s；計算：climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2354.4 kW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=300000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s; calculation: climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2354.4 kW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b315-v16-11","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gradient resistance and climbing power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。 由高程剖面核對坡度，使用同一時間窗比對速度與牽引功率，另列非重力負載。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent. Check gradient from the elevation profile, compare speed and traction power over one time window, and list non-gravitational loads separately. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用相同高差設計長緩坡與短陡坡，對比理想位能和峰值功率，指出兩者為何不能用同一項設備額定值評估。 再以本單元 mass 的對照值重算 climbing，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Design a long gentle and short steep climb with equal height gain, compare ideal energy and peak power, and explain why one equipment rating cannot evaluate both. Also recalculate climbing for the alternative mass value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating; a gradient-sign error can mislabel an energy-consuming section as regenerative. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。 由高程剖面核對坡度，使用同一時間窗比對速度與牽引功率，另列非重力負載。","textEn":"Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent. Check gradient from the elevation profile, compare speed and traction power over one time window, and list non-gravitational loads separately.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用相同高差設計長緩坡與短陡坡，對比理想位能和峰值功率，指出兩者為何不能用同一項設備額定值評估。 再以本單元 mass 的對照值重算 climbing，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Design a long gentle and short steep climb with equal height gain, compare ideal energy and peak power, and explain why one equipment rating cannot evaluate both. Also recalculate climbing for the alternative mass value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低","以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.","Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b315-v16-12","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gradient resistance and climbing power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。 功率不足時須分辨坡度阻力與黏著限制，不能只加大電流。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating; a gradient-sign error can mislabel an energy-consuming section as regenerative. When power is insufficient, distinguish gradient resistance from adhesion limits rather than only increasing current. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：對長坡計算持續重力功率，另列加速與空氣阻力需求。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Calculate sustained gravitational power on a long climb and separately list acceleration and drag demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。 功率不足時須分辨坡度阻力與黏著限制，不能只加大電流。","textEn":"Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating; a gradient-sign error can mislabel an energy-consuming section as regenerative. When power is insufficient, distinguish gradient resistance from adhesion limits rather than only increasing current.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating; a gradient-sign error can mislabel an energy-consuming section as regenerative. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b315-v16-13","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「黏著限制與可用牽引力」如何影響武漢—廣州高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Adhesion limit and usable traction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wuhan–Guangzhou high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"牽引力需要透過接觸斑傳到軌道，簡化上限與黏著係數及動輪法向力相乘。電機能提供更大扭矩不代表輪軌能傳遞；雨水、落葉與速度都會改變接觸狀態，使固定係數模型失去精度。 法向荷重應只取實際驅動接觸點的總量，不能自動使用整列重量。此上限也不描述黏著峰後的滑移控制；若輪重轉移，就要以每個接觸點重新分配。 把降雨前後輪軌接觸分組，避免用乾軌係數代表濕軌。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「黏著限制與可用牽引力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Traction reaches the track through contact patches. A simple upper bound multiplies adhesion coefficient by normal force on driven wheels. More motor torque does not guarantee more transmitted force; rain, leaves and speed alter contact conditions and limit the accuracy of a fixed coefficient. Normal load must include only the driven contacts, not automatically the weight of the whole train. This bound does not describe slip control beyond the adhesion peak. Wheel-load transfer requires a new allocation across individual contact points. Group contact conditions before and after rainfall instead of representing wet rails with a dry coefficient. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Adhesion limit and usable traction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N；計算：traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N; calculation: traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「黏著限制與可用牽引力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Adhesion limit and usable traction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-13-k1","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction","text":"牽引力需要透過接觸斑傳到軌道，簡化上限與黏著係數及動輪法向力相乘。電機能提供更大扭矩不代表輪軌能傳遞；雨水、落葉與速度都會改變接觸狀態，使固定係數模型失去精度。","textEn":"Traction reaches the track through contact patches. A simple upper bound multiplies adhesion coefficient by normal force on driven wheels.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「黏著限制與可用牽引力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\" is correct?","options":["電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著","牽引力需要透過接觸斑傳到軌道，簡化上限與黏著係數及動輪法向力相乘。","支承越柔軟所有頻率的振動就一定越小"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.","Traction reaches the track through contact patches.","Softer supports necessarily reduce vibration at every frequency."],"answer":1,"explanation":"牽引力需要透過接觸斑傳到軌道，簡化上限與黏著係數及動輪法向力相乘。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Traction reaches the track through contact patches. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b315-v16-14","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力：定量估算","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「黏著限制與可用牽引力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Adhesion limit and usable traction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N；計算：traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN。敏感度：mu 單獨增加百分之十至 0.198 1，其餘固定，結果為 178.2 kN。模型邊界：準靜態庫倫上限與均勻輪重；未建模蠕滑曲線及動態減載。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N; calculation: traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN. Sensitivity: mu, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.198 1, with all other inputs fixed, gives 178.2 kN. Model boundary: Quasi-static Coulomb bound with uniform wheel load; creep curves and dynamic unloading are not modelled. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N；計算：traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN。敏感度：mu 單獨增加百分之十至 0.198 1，其餘固定，結果為 178.2 kN。模型邊界：準靜態庫倫上限與均勻輪重；未建模蠕滑曲線及動態減載。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N; calculation: traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN. Sensitivity: mu, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.198 1, with all other inputs fixed, gives 178.2 kN. Model boundary: Quasi-static Coulomb bound with uniform wheel load; creep curves and dynamic unloading are not modelled.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「黏著限制與可用牽引力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\", which statement holds?","options":["煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點","用平均電流代入平方損耗公式總能得到正確熱負荷","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N。"],"optionsEn":["A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots.","Squaring average current always gives the correct resistive heat load.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N；計算：traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N; calculation: traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b315-v16-15","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「黏著限制與可用牽引力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Adhesion limit and usable traction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。 以獨立地速校對輪周速度，核實輪徑設定，再按乾濕條件與軸荷分類比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean. Calibrate wheel-periphery speed against independent ground speed, verify wheel-diameter settings, and compare results by wetness condition and axle load. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把黏著係數減半並比較動輪荷重調整，計算牽引上限，解釋為何撒砂或控制策略的效果需用試驗而不能只看馬達功率。 再以本單元 mu 的對照值重算 traction，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve adhesion and compare a change in driven-wheel load, calculate traction bounds, and explain why sanding or control performance requires tests rather than motor-power data alone. Also recalculate traction for the alternative mu value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction; an incorrect wheel diameter also creates apparent slip, requiring independent ground-speed evidence. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。 以獨立地速校對輪周速度，核實輪徑設定，再按乾濕條件與軸荷分類比對。","textEn":"Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean. Calibrate wheel-periphery speed against independent ground speed, verify wheel-diameter settings, and compare results by wetness condition and axle load.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把黏著係數減半並比較動輪荷重調整，計算牽引上限，解釋為何撒砂或控制策略的效果需用試驗而不能只看馬達功率。 再以本單元 mu 的對照值重算 traction，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Halve adhesion and compare a change in driven-wheel load, calculate traction bounds, and explain why sanding or control performance requires tests rather than motor-power data alone. Also recalculate traction for the alternative mu value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「黏著限制與可用牽引力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\"?","options":["比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位"],"optionsEn":["Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b315-v16-16","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「黏著限制與可用牽引力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Adhesion limit and usable traction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。 先查輪徑與地速誤差，避免把量測偏差當成真滑轉。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction; an incorrect wheel diameter also creates apparent slip, requiring independent ground-speed evidence. Check diameter and ground-speed errors before interpreting measurement bias as actual wheel slip. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把降雨前後輪軌接觸分組，避免用乾軌係數代表濕軌。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Group contact conditions before and after rainfall instead of representing wet rails with a dry coefficient.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。 先查輪徑與地速誤差，避免把量測偏差當成真滑轉。","textEn":"Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction; an incorrect wheel diameter also creates apparent slip, requiring independent ground-speed evidence. Check diameter and ground-speed errors before interpreting measurement bias as actual wheel slip.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「黏著限制與可用牽引力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。","支承越柔軟所有頻率的振動就一定越小"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction.","Softer supports necessarily reduce vibration at every frequency."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction; an incorrect wheel diameter also creates apparent slip, requiring independent ground-speed evidence. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b315-v16-s3","title":"振動隔離與頻率比與延遲與制動距離","titleEn":"Vibration isolation and frequency ratio & Delay and braking distance","description":"本階段聚焦「振動隔離與頻率比」與「延遲與制動距離」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Vibration isolation and frequency ratio\" and \"Delay and braking distance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b315-v16-17","title":"振動隔離與頻率比：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Vibration isolation and frequency ratio: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「振動隔離與頻率比」如何影響武漢—廣州高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Vibration isolation and frequency ratio” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wuhan–Guangzhou high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"浮動道床可用彈簧質量阻尼器理解，其隔振效果取決於激振頻率與固有頻率的比值。接近共振時柔軟支承反而會放大響應，超過隔振區後才可能衰減；靜態撓度與動態效果需要同時檢查。 此式描述單自由度線性隔振系統的力傳遞率，頻率比是激振頻率除以固有頻率。增加阻尼有助於抑制共振，但在高頻隔振區不一定降低傳遞；必須先辨認工況所在區域。 在隧道設備基座檢查振動隔離的頻率比，區分共振與高頻隔振。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「振動隔離與頻率比」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A floating track slab can be understood as a spring-mass-damper system whose isolation depends on excitation-to-natural-frequency ratio. Soft support can amplify response near resonance before attenuating higher frequencies. Static deflection and dynamic performance therefore need to be checked together. This expression describes force transmissibility of a linear single-degree-of-freedom isolator. Frequency ratio is excitation frequency divided by natural frequency. Added damping suppresses resonance but need not reduce transmission in the high-frequency isolation region, so identify the operating region first. Check frequency ratio for a tunnel-equipment isolator and distinguish resonance from high-frequency isolation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Vibration isolation and frequency ratio” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：ratio=3 1; zeta=0.12 1；計算：transmissibility=((1+(2*zeta*ratio)**2)/((1-ratio**2)**2+(2*zeta*ratio)**2))**0.5=0.1534092 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: ratio=3 1; zeta=0.12 1; calculation: transmissibility=((1+(2*zeta*ratio)**2)/((1-ratio**2)**2+(2*zeta*ratio)**2))**0.5=0.1534092 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「支承越柔軟所有頻率的振動就一定越小」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Softer supports necessarily reduce vibration at every frequency.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「振動隔離與頻率比」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Vibration isolation and frequency ratio”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-17-k1","title":"振動隔離與頻率比","titleEn":"Vibration isolation and frequency ratio","text":"浮動道床可用彈簧質量阻尼器理解，其隔振效果取決於激振頻率與固有頻率的比值。接近共振時柔軟支承反而會放大響應，超過隔振區後才可能衰減；靜態撓度與動態效果需要同時檢查。","textEn":"A floating track slab can be understood as a spring-mass-damper system whose isolation depends on excitation-to-natural-frequency ratio. Soft support can amplify response near resonance before attenuating higher frequencies.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：支承越柔軟所有頻率的振動就一定越小 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Softer supports necessarily reduce vibration at every frequency. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「振動隔離與頻率比」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Vibration isolation and frequency ratio\" is correct?","options":["支承越柔軟所有頻率的振動就一定越小","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成","浮動道床可用彈簧質量阻尼器理解，其隔振效果取決於激振頻率與固有頻率的比值。"],"optionsEn":["Softer supports necessarily reduce vibration at every frequency.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.","A floating track slab can be understood as a spring-mass-damper system whose isolation depends on excitation-to-natural-frequency ratio."],"answer":2,"explanation":"浮動道床可用彈簧質量阻尼器理解，其隔振效果取決於激振頻率與固有頻率的比值。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A floating track slab can be understood as a spring-mass-damper system whose isolation depends on excitation-to-natural-frequency ratio. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b315-v16-18","title":"振動隔離與頻率比：定量估算","titleEn":"Vibration isolation and frequency ratio: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「振動隔離與頻率比」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Vibration isolation and frequency ratio” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：ratio=3 1; zeta=0.12 1；計算：transmissibility=((1+(2*zeta*ratio)**2)/((1-ratio**2)**2+(2*zeta*ratio)**2))**0.5=0.1534092 1。敏感度：ratio 單獨增加百分之十至 3.3 1，其餘固定，結果為 0.1285715 1。模型邊界：線性單自由度力傳遞率；不含土層波傳、側向耦合及建築響應。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: ratio=3 1; zeta=0.12 1; calculation: transmissibility=((1+(2*zeta*ratio)**2)/((1-ratio**2)**2+(2*zeta*ratio)**2))**0.5=0.1534092 1. Sensitivity: ratio, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 3.3 1, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.1285715 1. Model boundary: Linear single-degree-of-freedom force transmissibility; soil propagation, lateral coupling and building response are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測軌道、道床與鄰近結構振動，使用頻譜比值而非只比較總加速度，並記錄列車速度與載重。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure rail, slab and neighbouring-structure vibration synchronously, compare spectra rather than only overall acceleration, and retain train speed and load.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：ratio=3 1; zeta=0.12 1；計算：transmissibility=((1+(2*zeta*ratio)**2)/((1-ratio**2)**2+(2*zeta*ratio)**2))**0.5=0.1534092 1。敏感度：ratio 單獨增加百分之十至 3.3 1，其餘固定，結果為 0.1285715 1。模型邊界：線性單自由度力傳遞率；不含土層波傳、側向耦合及建築響應。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: ratio=3 1; zeta=0.12 1; calculation: transmissibility=((1+(2*zeta*ratio)**2)/((1-ratio**2)**2+(2*zeta*ratio)**2))**0.5=0.1534092 1. Sensitivity: ratio, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 3.3 1, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.1285715 1. Model boundary: Linear single-degree-of-freedom force transmissibility; soil propagation, lateral coupling and building response are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「振動隔離與頻率比」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Vibration isolation and frequency ratio\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：ratio=3 1; zeta=0.12 1。","濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好","設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition.","High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：ratio=3 1; zeta=0.12 1；計算：transmissibility=((1+(2*zeta*ratio)**2)/((1-ratio**2)**2+(2*zeta*ratio)**2))**0.5=0.1534092 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: ratio=3 1; zeta=0.12 1; calculation: transmissibility=((1+(2*zeta*ratio)**2)/((1-ratio**2)**2+(2*zeta*ratio)**2))**0.5=0.1534092 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b315-v16-19","title":"振動隔離與頻率比：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Vibration isolation and frequency ratio: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「振動隔離與頻率比」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Vibration isolation and frequency ratio” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測軌道、道床與鄰近結構振動，使用頻譜比值而非只比較總加速度，並記錄列車速度與載重。 同步量測基座與支承反力頻譜，核對激振頻率、固有頻率和阻尼，檢查兩測點相位。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure rail, slab and neighbouring-structure vibration synchronously, compare spectra rather than only overall acceleration, and retain train speed and load. Measure base and transmitted-force spectra synchronously, verifying excitation frequency, natural frequency and damping while checking phase between measurement points. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：計算接近共振與高頻兩種頻率比，畫出傳遞率趨勢，提出能辨別材料硬化與剛性短路的量測位置。 再以本單元 ratio 的對照值重算 transmissibility，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate near-resonant and high-frequency ratios, plot the transmission trend, and propose sensor locations distinguishing material hardening from a rigid bypass. Also recalculate transmissibility for the alternative ratio value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：隔振墊硬化會提高固有頻率，局部短路接觸則繞過彈性路徑；兩者都可能讓預期隔振頻段失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Pad hardening raises natural frequency, while a rigid local contact bypasses the elastic path; either can remove the intended isolation band. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測軌道、道床與鄰近結構振動，使用頻譜比值而非只比較總加速度，並記錄列車速度與載重。 同步量測基座與支承反力頻譜，核對激振頻率、固有頻率和阻尼，檢查兩測點相位。","textEn":"Measure rail, slab and neighbouring-structure vibration synchronously, compare spectra rather than only overall acceleration, and retain train speed and load. Measure base and transmitted-force spectra synchronously, verifying excitation frequency, natural frequency and damping while checking phase between measurement points.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"計算接近共振與高頻兩種頻率比，畫出傳遞率趨勢，提出能辨別材料硬化與剛性短路的量測位置。 再以本單元 ratio 的對照值重算 transmissibility，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Calculate near-resonant and high-frequency ratios, plot the transmission trend, and propose sensor locations distinguishing material hardening from a rigid bypass. Also recalculate transmissibility for the alternative ratio value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「振動隔離與頻率比」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Vibration isolation and frequency ratio\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","同步量測軌道、道床與鄰近結構振動，使用頻譜比值而非只比較總加速度，並記錄列車速度與載重。","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure rail, slab and neighbouring-structure vibration synchronously, compare spectra rather than only overall acceleration, and retain train speed and load.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步量測軌道、道床與鄰近結構振動，使用頻譜比值而非只比較總加速度，並記錄列車速度與載重。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure rail, slab and neighbouring-structure vibration synchronously, compare spectra rather than only overall acceleration, and retain train speed and load. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b315-v16-20","title":"振動隔離與頻率比：失效診斷","titleEn":"Vibration isolation and frequency ratio: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「振動隔離與頻率比」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Vibration isolation and frequency ratio” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"隔振墊硬化會提高固有頻率，局部短路接觸則繞過彈性路徑；兩者都可能讓預期隔振頻段失效。 阻尼器劣化與剛度改變會有不同頻譜，須分開辨識。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Pad hardening raises natural frequency, while a rigid local contact bypasses the elastic path; either can remove the intended isolation band. Damper deterioration and stiffness change produce different spectral effects and must be identified separately. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在隧道設備基座檢查振動隔離的頻率比，區分共振與高頻隔振。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Check frequency ratio for a tunnel-equipment isolator and distinguish resonance from high-frequency isolation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「支承越柔軟所有頻率的振動就一定越小」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Softer supports necessarily reduce vibration at every frequency.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"隔振墊硬化會提高固有頻率，局部短路接觸則繞過彈性路徑；兩者都可能讓預期隔振頻段失效。 阻尼器劣化與剛度改變會有不同頻譜，須分開辨識。","textEn":"Pad hardening raises natural frequency, while a rigid local contact bypasses the elastic path; either can remove the intended isolation band. Damper deterioration and stiffness change produce different spectral effects and must be identified separately.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「振動隔離與頻率比」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Vibration isolation and frequency ratio\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成","隔振墊硬化會提高固有頻率，局部短路接觸則繞過彈性路徑；兩者都可能讓預期隔振頻段失效。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.","Pad hardening raises natural frequency, while a rigid local contact bypasses the elastic path; either can remove the intended isolation band."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隔振墊硬化會提高固有頻率，局部短路接觸則繞過彈性路徑；兩者都可能讓預期隔振頻段失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Pad hardening raises natural frequency, while a rigid local contact bypasses the elastic path; either can remove the intended isolation band. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b315-v16-21","title":"延遲與制動距離：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「延遲與制動距離」如何影響武漢—廣州高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Delay and braking distance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wuhan–Guangzhou high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車在控制命令傳遞與煞車建立期間仍向前行駛，減速段才把動能耗散；因此停車距離包含延遲距離與減速距離。速度平方項說明高速時少量速度誤差會被放大，固定減速度只能作第一輪界限估算。 延遲項與速度成正比，減速項與速度平方成正比；把兩項分開後，才能選擇改善控制延遲或增加有效制動的方案。若存在坡度，應另加沿坡重力，不能只改總距離。 對低黏著降速情境重算停車距離與命令延遲。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「延遲與制動距離」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A train continues moving while the command propagates and brake force builds. Only the deceleration phase removes kinetic energy, so stopping distance includes both a delay term and a braking term. The squared speed dependence amplifies speed uncertainty; constant deceleration is only an initial bounding approximation. The delay term is linear in speed and the deceleration term is quadratic. Separating them reveals whether control latency or effective braking deserves attention. A gradient requires an added gravitational component, not an arbitrary adjustment to the final distance. Recalculate stopping distance and command delay for a low-adhesion restricted-speed condition. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Delay and braking distance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2；計算：distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2; calculation: distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「延遲與制動距離」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Delay and braking distance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-21-k1","title":"延遲與制動距離","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance","text":"列車在控制命令傳遞與煞車建立期間仍向前行駛，減速段才把動能耗散；因此停車距離包含延遲距離與減速距離。速度平方項說明高速時少量速度誤差會被放大，固定減速度只能作第一輪界限估算。","textEn":"A train continues moving while the command propagates and brake force builds. Only the deceleration phase removes kinetic energy, so stopping distance includes both a delay term and a braking term.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「延遲與制動距離」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Delay and braking distance\" is correct?","options":["列車在控制命令傳遞與煞車建立期間仍向前行駛，減速段才把動能耗散；因此停車距離包含延遲距離與減速距離。","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成","煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點"],"optionsEn":["A train continues moving while the command propagates and brake force builds.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.","A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots."],"answer":0,"explanation":"列車在控制命令傳遞與煞車建立期間仍向前行駛，減速段才把動能耗散；因此停車距離包含延遲距離與減速距離。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A train continues moving while the command propagates and brake force builds. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b315-v16-22","title":"延遲與制動距離：定量估算","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「延遲與制動距離」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Delay and braking distance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2；計算：distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m。敏感度：v 單獨增加百分之十至 77 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 4427.5 m。模型邊界：水平直線、定減速、無風；沒有建立黏著分布與煞車熱衰退。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2; calculation: distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m. Sensitivity: v, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 77 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 4427.5 m. Model boundary: Level straight track and constant deceleration; adhesion variation and thermal fade are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2；計算：distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m。敏感度：v 單獨增加百分之十至 77 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 4427.5 m。模型邊界：水平直線、定減速、無風；沒有建立黏著分布與煞車熱衰退。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2; calculation: distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m. Sensitivity: v, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 77 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 4427.5 m. Model boundary: Level straight track and constant deceleration; adhesion variation and thermal fade are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「延遲與制動距離」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Delay and braking distance\", which statement holds?","options":["用平均電流代入平方損耗公式總能得到正確熱負荷","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位"],"optionsEn":["Squaring average current always gives the correct resistive heat load.","Original hypothetical exercise.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2；計算：distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2; calculation: distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b315-v16-23","title":"延遲與制動距離：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「延遲與制動距離」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Delay and braking distance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。 用獨立里程或地速核對輪速積分，報告濕乾軌差異及停車距離的重複試驗範圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps. Identify command delay separately from steady deceleration and cross-check distance by integrating measured speed. Check integrated wheel speed against independent distance or ground speed, and report wet-dry differences and repeated stopping-distance ranges. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別增加延遲與初速，畫出兩條停車曲線；寫出哪個區段對各參數敏感，以及需要哪些現場資料才可建立保護曲線。 再以本單元 v 的對照值重算 distance，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase delay and initial speed separately, plot both stopping curves, identify the sensitive phase, and list the field evidence needed before defining a protection curve. Also recalculate distance for the alternative v value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration; unsynchronised sensors can imitate a delay, requiring an independent clock and wheel-speed records. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。 用獨立里程或地速核對輪速積分，報告濕乾軌差異及停車距離的重複試驗範圍。","textEn":"Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps. Identify command delay separately from steady deceleration and cross-check distance by integrating measured speed. Check integrated wheel speed against independent distance or ground speed, and report wet-dry differences and repeated stopping-distance ranges.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別增加延遲與初速，畫出兩條停車曲線；寫出哪個區段對各參數敏感，以及需要哪些現場資料才可建立保護曲線。 再以本單元 v 的對照值重算 distance，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase delay and initial speed separately, plot both stopping curves, identify the sensitive phase, and list the field evidence needed before defining a protection curve. Also recalculate distance for the alternative v value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「延遲與制動距離」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Delay and braking distance\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動","對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.","Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b315-v16-24","title":"延遲與制動距離：失效診斷","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「延遲與制動距離」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Delay and braking distance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。 應比較壓力建立與地速下降先後，避免誤判煞車故障。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration; unsynchronised sensors can imitate a delay, requiring an independent clock and wheel-speed records. Compare pressure build-up with ground-speed decay before diagnosing a brake fault. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：對低黏著降速情境重算停車距離與命令延遲。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Recalculate stopping distance and command delay for a low-adhesion restricted-speed condition.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。 應比較壓力建立與地速下降先後，避免誤判煞車故障。","textEn":"Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration; unsynchronised sensors can imitate a delay, requiring an independent clock and wheel-speed records. Compare pressure build-up with ground-speed decay before diagnosing a brake fault.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「延遲與制動距離」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Delay and braking distance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點"],"optionsEn":["Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots."],"answer":0,"explanation":"輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration; unsynchronised sensors can imitate a delay, requiring an independent clock and wheel-speed records. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b315-v16-s4","title":"煞車熱量與溫升與濾網壓差與通風功率","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise & Filter pressure drop and fan power","description":"本階段聚焦「煞車熱量與溫升」與「濾網壓差與通風功率」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Brake heat and temperature rise\" and \"Filter pressure drop and fan power\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b315-v16-25","title":"煞車熱量與溫升：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「煞車熱量與溫升」如何影響武漢—廣州高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Brake heat and temperature rise” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wuhan–Guangzhou high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"未回收的動能會在摩擦煞車與阻力路徑中轉成熱，平均溫升由分配到構件的能量除以熱容量決定。短時平均模型無法描述表面熱點、對流冷卻或熱裂紋，需要把能量分配與熱擴散分開。 有效受熱質量可以小於構件總質量，短時接觸表面的熱量也未必已傳到內部。能量平衡應先界定摩擦分配比例，再評估對流、輻射和間歇冷卻是否可忽略。 在長下坡減速後估算煞車平均溫升並辨認熱點風險。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「煞車熱量與溫升」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Unrecovered kinetic energy becomes heat through friction brakes and resistance paths. Average temperature rise is allocated energy divided by thermal capacity. A short-duration lumped model cannot describe surface hot spots, cooling or thermal cracks; energy allocation and thermal diffusion are separate questions. The effective heated mass can be smaller than total component mass, and short-duration surface heat may not reach the interior. First define frictional energy allocation, then assess whether convection, radiation and cooling between events can be neglected. Estimate mean brake temperature rise after descending deceleration and identify hot-spot risk. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Brake heat and temperature rise” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.2e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)；計算：rise=energy/(mass*cp)=118.5771 K。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=1.2e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K); calculation: rise=energy/(mass*cp)=118.5771 K.","failure":"常見誤解：「煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「煞車熱量與溫升」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Brake heat and temperature rise”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-25-k1","title":"煞車熱量與溫升","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise","text":"未回收的動能會在摩擦煞車與阻力路徑中轉成熱，平均溫升由分配到構件的能量除以熱容量決定。短時平均模型無法描述表面熱點、對流冷卻或熱裂紋，需要把能量分配與熱擴散分開。","textEn":"Unrecovered kinetic energy becomes heat through friction brakes and resistance paths. Average temperature rise is allocated energy divided by thermal capacity.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「煞車熱量與溫升」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Brake heat and temperature rise\" is correct?","options":["煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點","未回收的動能會在摩擦煞車與阻力路徑中轉成熱，平均溫升由分配到構件的能量除以熱容量決定。","濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好"],"optionsEn":["A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots.","Unrecovered kinetic energy becomes heat through friction brakes and resistance paths.","Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"未回收的動能會在摩擦煞車與阻力路徑中轉成熱，平均溫升由分配到構件的能量除以熱容量決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Unrecovered kinetic energy becomes heat through friction brakes and resistance paths. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b315-v16-26","title":"煞車熱量與溫升：定量估算","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「煞車熱量與溫升」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Brake heat and temperature rise” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.2e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)；計算：rise=energy/(mass*cp)=118.5771 K。敏感度：energy 單獨增加百分之十至 1.32e+07 J，其餘固定，結果為 130.4348 K。模型邊界：均勻溫度且無散熱、常數比熱；不推定摩擦材極限。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=1.2e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K); calculation: rise=energy/(mass*cp)=118.5771 K. Sensitivity: energy, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1.32e+07 J, with all other inputs fixed, gives 130.4348 K. Model boundary: Uniform temperature without heat loss and with constant heat capacity; no friction-material limit is inferred. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.2e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)；計算：rise=energy/(mass*cp)=118.5771 K。敏感度：energy 單獨增加百分之十至 1.32e+07 J，其餘固定，結果為 130.4348 K。模型邊界：均勻溫度且無散熱、常數比熱；不推定摩擦材極限。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=1.2e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K); calculation: rise=energy/(mass*cp)=118.5771 K. Sensitivity: energy, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1.32e+07 J, with all other inputs fixed, gives 130.4348 K. Model boundary: Uniform temperature without heat loss and with constant heat capacity; no friction-material limit is inferred.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「煞車熱量與溫升」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Brake heat and temperature rise\", which statement holds?","options":["設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.2e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)。"],"optionsEn":["High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.2e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)；計算：rise=energy/(mass*cp)=118.5771 K。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=1.2e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K); calculation: rise=energy/(mass*cp)=118.5771 K. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b315-v16-27","title":"煞車熱量與溫升：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「煞車熱量與溫升」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Brake heat and temperature rise” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。 在不同深度保留溫度曲線並核對感測器反應時間，用初末能量平衡檢查平均溫升。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity. Retain temperature histories at different depths, verify sensor response time, and use initial-to-final energy balance to check mean temperature rise. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將同一能量分給兩種有效熱容量，計算平均溫升後設計能辨認熱點的量測網格，說明集中參數模型缺少哪些資訊。 再以本單元 energy 的對照值重算 rise，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Allocate equal energy to two effective thermal capacities, calculate average rise, and design a measurement grid for hot spots while identifying information missing from the lumped model. Also recalculate rise for the alternative energy value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。 在不同深度保留溫度曲線並核對感測器反應時間，用初末能量平衡檢查平均溫升。","textEn":"Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity. Retain temperature histories at different depths, verify sensor response time, and use initial-to-final energy balance to check mean temperature rise.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將同一能量分給兩種有效熱容量，計算平均溫升後設計能辨認熱點的量測網格，說明集中參數模型缺少哪些資訊。 再以本單元 energy 的對照值重算 rise，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Allocate equal energy to two effective thermal capacities, calculate average rise, and design a measurement grid for hot spots while identifying information missing from the lumped model. Also recalculate rise for the alternative energy value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「煞車熱量與溫升」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Brake heat and temperature rise\"?","options":["以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著"],"optionsEn":["Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b315-v16-28","title":"煞車熱量與溫升：失效診斷","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「煞車熱量與溫升」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Brake heat and temperature rise” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。 若表面與內部溫差很大，集中熱容量假設便不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature. A large surface-to-core temperature difference indicates that the lumped thermal-capacity assumption is insufficient. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在長下坡減速後估算煞車平均溫升並辨認熱點風險。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Estimate mean brake temperature rise after descending deceleration and identify hot-spot risk.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。 若表面與內部溫差很大，集中熱容量假設便不足。","textEn":"Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature. A large surface-to-core temperature difference indicates that the lumped thermal-capacity assumption is insufficient.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「煞車熱量與溫升」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Brake heat and temperature rise\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。","濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature.","Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b315-v16-29","title":"濾網壓差與通風功率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Filter pressure drop and fan power: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「濾網壓差與通風功率」如何影響武漢—廣州高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Filter pressure drop and fan power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wuhan–Guangzhou high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"風機必須克服風道與濾網壓差才能輸送空氣，輸入功率近似為壓差乘體積流率再除效率。積塵提高阻力但工作點會沿風機曲線改變，因此固定風量假設只是一種受控比較。 風機功率等於壓力差乘體積流率再除以宣告效率，壓力與流量必須使用同一工作點。積塵使阻力和風機工作點共同改變，固定流量算例不能預測未控制風量時的耗電。 檢查濕濾材造成的壓差是否隨風量變動而改變判讀。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「濾網壓差與通風功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A fan must overcome duct and filter pressure losses to move air. Input power is approximately pressure rise times volume flow divided by efficiency. Dust raises resistance but shifts the operating point on the fan curve, so fixed flow is only a controlled comparison. Fan power equals pressure difference times volume flow divided by the declared efficiency. Pressure and flow must refer to one operating point. Dust changes resistance and the fan operating point together, so a fixed-flow example cannot predict consumption without airflow control. Check whether changing airflow confounds interpretation of pressure drop across wet filter media. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Filter pressure drop and fan power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1；計算：fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1; calculation: fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W.","failure":"常見誤解：「濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「濾網壓差與通風功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Filter pressure drop and fan power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-29-k1","title":"濾網壓差與通風功率","titleEn":"Filter pressure drop and fan power","text":"風機必須克服風道與濾網壓差才能輸送空氣，輸入功率近似為壓差乘體積流率再除效率。積塵提高阻力但工作點會沿風機曲線改變，因此固定風量假設只是一種受控比較。","textEn":"A fan must overcome duct and filter pressure losses to move air. Input power is approximately pressure rise times volume flow divided by efficiency.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「濾網壓差與通風功率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Filter pressure drop and fan power\" is correct?","options":["濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好","用平均電流代入平方損耗公式總能得到正確熱負荷","風機必須克服風道與濾網壓差才能輸送空氣，輸入功率近似為壓差乘體積流率再除效率。"],"optionsEn":["Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition.","Squaring average current always gives the correct resistive heat load.","A fan must overcome duct and filter pressure losses to move air."],"answer":2,"explanation":"風機必須克服風道與濾網壓差才能輸送空氣，輸入功率近似為壓差乘體積流率再除效率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A fan must overcome duct and filter pressure losses to move air. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b315-v16-30","title":"濾網壓差與通風功率：定量估算","titleEn":"Filter pressure drop and fan power: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「濾網壓差與通風功率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Filter pressure drop and fan power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1；計算：fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W。敏感度：pressure 單獨增加百分之十至 385 Pa，其餘固定，結果為 1604.167 W。模型邊界：固定風量與總效率；不包含風機曲線移動和馬達熱限制。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1; calculation: fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W. Sensitivity: pressure, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 385 Pa, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1604.167 W. Model boundary: Fixed flow and overall efficiency; fan-curve shifts and motor thermal limits are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時量濾網前後壓差、實際風量和電功率，用乾淨濾網建立基準，並記錄沙塵、濕度與維修時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure differential pressure, actual flow and input power together, establish a clean-filter baseline, and record dust exposure, humidity and maintenance timing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1；計算：fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W。敏感度：pressure 單獨增加百分之十至 385 Pa，其餘固定，結果為 1604.167 W。模型邊界：固定風量與總效率；不包含風機曲線移動和馬達熱限制。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1; calculation: fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W. Sensitivity: pressure, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 385 Pa, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1604.167 W. Model boundary: Fixed flow and overall efficiency; fan-curve shifts and motor thermal limits are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「濾網壓差與通風功率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Filter pressure drop and fan power\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1；計算：fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1; calculation: fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b315-v16-31","title":"濾網壓差與通風功率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Filter pressure drop and fan power: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「濾網壓差與通風功率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Filter pressure drop and fan power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時量濾網前後壓差、實際風量和電功率，用乾淨濾網建立基準，並記錄沙塵、濕度與維修時間。 校正取壓點與風量計，同步量測電功率，核對效率是否包含馬達與驅動器損失。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure differential pressure, actual flow and input power together, establish a clean-filter baseline, and record dust exposure, humidity and maintenance timing. Calibrate pressure taps and airflow measurement, record electric power simultaneously, and check whether efficiency includes motor and drive losses. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對堵塞與旁路兩個情境列出壓差、風量和粒子濃度的預期方向，設計三項量測共同判斷而非只靠單一數字。 再以本單元 pressure 的對照值重算 fan_power，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Predict pressure drop, airflow and particle concentration for clogging and bypass scenarios, then design a three-measurement diagnosis instead of relying on one number. Also recalculate fan_power for the alternative pressure value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：旁路漏氣可能讓壓差降低但過濾品質變差；只以壓差低判定良好，會忽略濾網破損和密封失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Bypass leakage may lower pressure drop while worsening filtration; a low drop alone can therefore hide a damaged filter or failed seal. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時量濾網前後壓差、實際風量和電功率，用乾淨濾網建立基準，並記錄沙塵、濕度與維修時間。 校正取壓點與風量計，同步量測電功率，核對效率是否包含馬達與驅動器損失。","textEn":"Measure differential pressure, actual flow and input power together, establish a clean-filter baseline, and record dust exposure, humidity and maintenance timing. Calibrate pressure taps and airflow measurement, record electric power simultaneously, and check whether efficiency includes motor and drive losses.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對堵塞與旁路兩個情境列出壓差、風量和粒子濃度的預期方向，設計三項量測共同判斷而非只靠單一數字。 再以本單元 pressure 的對照值重算 fan_power，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Predict pressure drop, airflow and particle concentration for clogging and bypass scenarios, then design a three-measurement diagnosis instead of relying on one number. Also recalculate fan_power for the alternative pressure value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「濾網壓差與通風功率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Filter pressure drop and fan power\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","同時量濾網前後壓差、實際風量和電功率，用乾淨濾網建立基準，並記錄沙塵、濕度與維修時間。","支承越柔軟所有頻率的振動就一定越小"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Measure differential pressure, actual flow and input power together, establish a clean-filter baseline, and record dust exposure, humidity and maintenance timing.","Softer supports necessarily reduce vibration at every frequency."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同時量濾網前後壓差、實際風量和電功率，用乾淨濾網建立基準，並記錄沙塵、濕度與維修時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure differential pressure, actual flow and input power together, establish a clean-filter baseline, and record dust exposure, humidity and maintenance timing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b315-v16-32","title":"濾網壓差與通風功率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Filter pressure drop and fan power: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「濾網壓差與通風功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Filter pressure drop and fan power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"旁路漏氣可能讓壓差降低但過濾品質變差；只以壓差低判定良好，會忽略濾網破損和密封失效。 壓差很低也可能是旁通，須核對濾材密封及實際風量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Bypass leakage may lower pressure drop while worsening filtration; a low drop alone can therefore hide a damaged filter or failed seal. Very low pressure drop can indicate bypass; check filter sealing and actual airflow. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：檢查濕濾材造成的壓差是否隨風量變動而改變判讀。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Check whether changing airflow confounds interpretation of pressure drop across wet filter media.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"旁路漏氣可能讓壓差降低但過濾品質變差；只以壓差低判定良好，會忽略濾網破損和密封失效。 壓差很低也可能是旁通，須核對濾材密封及實際風量。","textEn":"Bypass leakage may lower pressure drop while worsening filtration; a low drop alone can therefore hide a damaged filter or failed seal. Very low pressure drop can indicate bypass; check filter sealing and actual airflow.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「濾網壓差與通風功率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Filter pressure drop and fan power\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","用平均電流代入平方損耗公式總能得到正確熱負荷","旁路漏氣可能讓壓差降低但過濾品質變差；只以壓差低判定良好，會忽略濾網破損和密封失效。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Squaring average current always gives the correct resistive heat load.","Bypass leakage may lower pressure drop while worsening filtration; a low drop alone can therefore hide a damaged filter or failed seal."],"answer":2,"explanation":"旁路漏氣可能讓壓差降低但過濾品質變差；只以壓差低判定良好，會忽略濾網破損和密封失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Bypass leakage may lower pressure drop while worsening filtration; a low drop alone can therefore hide a damaged filter or failed seal. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b315-v16-s5","title":"電流平方損耗與散熱與可用度與修復時間","titleEn":"Current-squared losses and cooling & Availability and repair time","description":"本階段聚焦「電流平方損耗與散熱」與「可用度與修復時間」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Current-squared losses and cooling\" and \"Availability and repair time\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b315-v16-33","title":"電流平方損耗與散熱：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Current-squared losses and cooling: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「電流平方損耗與散熱」如何影響武漢—廣州高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Current-squared losses and cooling” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wuhan–Guangzhou high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"導體與接點的焦耳熱與電流平方成正比，短時高電流可能主導熱循環而平均電流看不出來。散熱取決於環境與接觸表面，電氣損耗量不能直接當成最終溫升。 此式是導體焦耳熱，並不是列車全部耗電。電阻會隨溫度改變，而並聯饋電使電流重新分配；比較兩方案時應保持相同功率交付邊界，避免只移轉損失位置。 在長距離供電段比較不同電流造成的線路熱損失。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「電流平方損耗與散熱」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Joule heating in conductors and joints scales with current squared, so short current peaks can dominate thermal cycling even when mean current looks moderate. Heat rejection depends on environment and contact surfaces; electrical loss alone is not a final temperature prediction. The expression represents conductor Joule heat, not all train consumption. Resistance changes with temperature, and parallel feeding redistributes current. Compare schemes at the same delivered-power boundary to avoid reporting loss relocation as an actual reduction. Compare line heating losses under different current levels in a long supply section. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Current-squared losses and cooling” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：current=1200 A; resistance=0.025 ohm；計算：loss=current*current*resistance/1000=36 kW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: current=1200 A; resistance=0.025 ohm; calculation: loss=current*current*resistance/1000=36 kW.","failure":"常見誤解：「用平均電流代入平方損耗公式總能得到正確熱負荷」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Squaring average current always gives the correct resistive heat load.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「電流平方損耗與散熱」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Current-squared losses and cooling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-33-k1","title":"電流平方損耗與散熱","titleEn":"Current-squared losses and cooling","text":"導體與接點的焦耳熱與電流平方成正比，短時高電流可能主導熱循環而平均電流看不出來。散熱取決於環境與接觸表面，電氣損耗量不能直接當成最終溫升。","textEn":"Joule heating in conductors and joints scales with current squared, so short current peaks can dominate thermal cycling even when mean current looks moderate. Heat rejection depends on environment and contact surfaces; electrical loss alone is not a final temperature prediction.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：用平均電流代入平方損耗公式總能得到正確熱負荷 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Squaring average current always gives the correct resistive heat load. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電流平方損耗與散熱」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Current-squared losses and cooling\" is correct?","options":["導體與接點的焦耳熱與電流平方成正比，短時高電流可能主導熱循環而平均電流看不出來。","用平均電流代入平方損耗公式總能得到正確熱負荷","設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低"],"optionsEn":["Joule heating in conductors and joints scales with current squared, so short current peaks can dominate thermal cycling even when mean current looks moderate.","Squaring average current always gives the correct resistive heat load.","High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low."],"answer":0,"explanation":"導體與接點的焦耳熱與電流平方成正比，短時高電流可能主導熱循環而平均電流看不出來。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Joule heating in conductors and joints scales with current squared, so short current peaks can dominate thermal cycling even when mean current looks moderate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b315-v16-34","title":"電流平方損耗與散熱：定量估算","titleEn":"Current-squared losses and cooling: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「電流平方損耗與散熱」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Current-squared losses and cooling” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：current=1200 A; resistance=0.025 ohm；計算：loss=current*current*resistance/1000=36 kW。敏感度：current 單獨增加百分之十至 1320 A，其餘固定，結果為 43.56 kW。模型邊界：恆定電阻且直流或等效均方根電流；不含散熱暫態。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: current=1200 A; resistance=0.025 ohm; calculation: loss=current*current*resistance/1000=36 kW. Sensitivity: current, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1320 A, with all other inputs fixed, gives 43.56 kW. Model boundary: Constant resistance with direct or equivalent RMS current; transient cooling is excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以均方根電流而非算術平均電流求熱負荷，同步記錄接頭溫度及環境；停電隔離後才由合格人員檢查接點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use RMS rather than arithmetic-mean current for thermal loading, log joint and ambient temperatures, and restrict physical inspection to qualified staff after isolation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：current=1200 A; resistance=0.025 ohm；計算：loss=current*current*resistance/1000=36 kW。敏感度：current 單獨增加百分之十至 1320 A，其餘固定，結果為 43.56 kW。模型邊界：恆定電阻且直流或等效均方根電流；不含散熱暫態。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: current=1200 A; resistance=0.025 ohm; calculation: loss=current*current*resistance/1000=36 kW. Sensitivity: current, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1320 A, with all other inputs fixed, gives 43.56 kW. Model boundary: Constant resistance with direct or equivalent RMS current; transient cooling is excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「電流平方損耗與散熱」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Current-squared losses and cooling\", which statement holds?","options":["隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：current=1200 A; resistance=0.025 ohm。","電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著"],"optionsEn":["A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.","Original hypothetical exercise.","A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：current=1200 A; resistance=0.025 ohm；計算：loss=current*current*resistance/1000=36 kW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: current=1200 A; resistance=0.025 ohm; calculation: loss=current*current*resistance/1000=36 kW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b315-v16-35","title":"電流平方損耗與散熱：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Current-squared losses and cooling: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「電流平方損耗與散熱」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Current-squared losses and cooling” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以均方根電流而非算術平均電流求熱負荷，同步記錄接頭溫度及環境；停電隔離後才由合格人員檢查接點。 由電流時間歷程積分損失，量測導體溫度以校正電阻，並比對兩端功率差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use RMS rather than arithmetic-mean current for thermal loading, log joint and ambient temperatures, and restrict physical inspection to qualified staff after isolation. Integrate losses over the current history, measure conductor temperature to correct resistance, and compare with the difference between terminal powers. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較固定電流與同平均值脈衝電流的均方根，計算兩種損耗，寫出溫度監測與電流紀錄需要同步的原因。 再以本單元 current 的對照值重算 loss，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare constant and pulsed currents with equal means, calculate their RMS losses, and explain why current and temperature records must be time-aligned. Also recalculate loss for the alternative current value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：鬆動接點會增加電阻並使熱量集中；熱像單次讀值偏低也可能只是量測時負載不高，不能否定間歇性過熱。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Loose joints increase resistance and concentrate heating; a cool one-time thermal image may simply coincide with low load and cannot rule out intermittent overheating. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以均方根電流而非算術平均電流求熱負荷，同步記錄接頭溫度及環境；停電隔離後才由合格人員檢查接點。 由電流時間歷程積分損失，量測導體溫度以校正電阻，並比對兩端功率差。","textEn":"Use RMS rather than arithmetic-mean current for thermal loading, log joint and ambient temperatures, and restrict physical inspection to qualified staff after isolation. Integrate losses over the current history, measure conductor temperature to correct resistance, and compare with the difference between terminal powers.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較固定電流與同平均值脈衝電流的均方根，計算兩種損耗，寫出溫度監測與電流紀錄需要同步的原因。 再以本單元 current 的對照值重算 loss，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare constant and pulsed currents with equal means, calculate their RMS losses, and explain why current and temperature records must be time-aligned. Also recalculate loss for the alternative current value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「電流平方損耗與散熱」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Current-squared losses and cooling\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成","以均方根電流而非算術平均電流求熱負荷，同步記錄接頭溫度及環境；停電隔離後才由合格人員檢查接點。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.","Use RMS rather than arithmetic-mean current for thermal loading, log joint and ambient temperatures, and restrict physical inspection to qualified staff after isolation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以均方根電流而非算術平均電流求熱負荷，同步記錄接頭溫度及環境；停電隔離後才由合格人員檢查接點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use RMS rather than arithmetic-mean current for thermal loading, log joint and ambient temperatures, and restrict physical inspection to qualified staff after isolation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b315-v16-36","title":"電流平方損耗與散熱：失效診斷","titleEn":"Current-squared losses and cooling: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「電流平方損耗與散熱」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Current-squared losses and cooling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"鬆動接點會增加電阻並使熱量集中；熱像單次讀值偏低也可能只是量測時負載不高，不能否定間歇性過熱。 尖峰電流不能用平均電流取代，否則平方項損失被低估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Loose joints increase resistance and concentrate heating; a cool one-time thermal image may simply coincide with low load and cannot rule out intermittent overheating. Peak current cannot be replaced by mean current without understating losses from the squared term. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在長距離供電段比較不同電流造成的線路熱損失。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare line heating losses under different current levels in a long supply section.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「用平均電流代入平方損耗公式總能得到正確熱負荷」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Squaring average current always gives the correct resistive heat load.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"鬆動接點會增加電阻並使熱量集中；熱像單次讀值偏低也可能只是量測時負載不高，不能否定間歇性過熱。 尖峰電流不能用平均電流取代，否則平方項損失被低估。","textEn":"Loose joints increase resistance and concentrate heating; a cool one-time thermal image may simply coincide with low load and cannot rule out intermittent overheating. Peak current cannot be replaced by mean current without understating losses from the squared term.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電流平方損耗與散熱」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Current-squared losses and cooling\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["鬆動接點會增加電阻並使熱量集中；熱像單次讀值偏低也可能只是量測時負載不高，不能否定間歇性過熱。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低"],"optionsEn":["Loose joints increase resistance and concentrate heating.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鬆動接點會增加電阻並使熱量集中；熱像單次讀值偏低也可能只是量測時負載不高，不能否定間歇性過熱。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Loose joints increase resistance and concentrate heating; a cool one-time thermal image may simply coincide with low load and cannot rule out intermittent overheating. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b315-v16-37","title":"可用度與修復時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Availability and repair time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「可用度與修復時間」如何影響武漢—廣州高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Availability and repair time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wuhan–Guangzhou high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"在簡化更新過程中，可用度是平均故障間隔占故障間隔加修復時間的比例。這個指標不能替代安全性，因為快速恢復服務可能仍保留危險失效；備品、交通與診斷都會影響實際修復時間。 平均故障間隔和平均修復時間必須使用相同服務邊界；備件等待與到場時間若被排除，數字就不能描述旅客看到的中斷。短期樣本也應報告事件數與觀測時間。 把防水維修時間與正常設備修復分別納入停機紀錄。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「可用度與修復時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In a simplified renewal process, availability is mean time between failures divided by that time plus mean repair time. It does not replace safety: rapidly restoring service may leave a hazardous failure unresolved. Spares, travel and diagnosis all affect actual restoration time. Mean time between failures and mean repair time require a common service boundary. Excluding spare-part waiting or travel time prevents the figure from describing passenger-visible interruption. Short samples should also report event count and observation duration. Record waterproofing maintenance separately from normal equipment repair in downtime records. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Availability and repair time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1200 h; mttr=4 h；計算：availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9966777 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mtbf=1200 h; mttr=4 h; calculation: availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9966777 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「可用度與修復時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Availability and repair time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-37-k1","title":"可用度與修復時間","titleEn":"Availability and repair time","text":"在簡化更新過程中，可用度是平均故障間隔占故障間隔加修復時間的比例。這個指標不能替代安全性，因為快速恢復服務可能仍保留危險失效；備品、交通與診斷都會影響實際修復時間。","textEn":"In a simplified renewal process, availability is mean time between failures divided by that time plus mean repair time. It does not replace safety: rapidly restoring service may leave a hazardous failure unresolved.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「可用度與修復時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Availability and repair time\" is correct?","options":["設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低","在簡化更新過程中，可用度是平均故障間隔占故障間隔加修復時間的比例。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位"],"optionsEn":["High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.","In a simplified renewal process, availability is mean time between failures divided by that time plus mean repair time.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在簡化更新過程中，可用度是平均故障間隔占故障間隔加修復時間的比例。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In a simplified renewal process, availability is mean time between failures divided by that time plus mean repair time. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b315-v16-38","title":"可用度與修復時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Availability and repair time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「可用度與修復時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Availability and repair time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1200 h; mttr=4 h；計算：availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9966777 1。敏感度：mtbf 單獨增加百分之十至 1320 h，其餘固定，結果為 0.9969789 1。模型邊界：兩狀態穩態平均模型；不含計畫維修、共同原因與降級服務品質。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mtbf=1200 h; mttr=4 h; calculation: availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9966777 1. Sensitivity: mtbf, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1320 h, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.9969789 1. Model boundary: Two-state steady-state mean model; planned maintenance, common causes and degraded service quality are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1200 h; mttr=4 h；計算：availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9966777 1。敏感度：mtbf 單獨增加百分之十至 1320 h，其餘固定，結果為 0.9969789 1。模型邊界：兩狀態穩態平均模型；不含計畫維修、共同原因與降級服務品質。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mtbf=1200 h; mttr=4 h; calculation: availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9966777 1. Sensitivity: mtbf, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1320 h, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.9969789 1. Model boundary: Two-state steady-state mean model; planned maintenance, common causes and degraded service quality are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「可用度與修復時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Availability and repair time\", which statement holds?","options":["長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動","支承越柔軟所有頻率的振動就一定越小","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1200 h; mttr=4 h。"],"optionsEn":["One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.","Softer supports necessarily reduce vibration at every frequency.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1200 h; mttr=4 h；計算：availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9966777 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mtbf=1200 h; mttr=4 h; calculation: availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9966777 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b315-v16-39","title":"可用度與修復時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Availability and repair time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「可用度與修復時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Availability and repair time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。 逐項對照故障開始、服務恢復與維修完成時間，公開排除項，並核對總觀測時數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service. Cross-check fault start, service restoration and repair completion for each event, disclose exclusions, and verify total observed hours. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較提高故障間隔與縮短修復時間兩種措施，用同一故障定義重算，並列出可用度之外需要追蹤的危險失效指標。 再以本單元 mtbf 的對照值重算 availability，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare increasing failure interval with reducing repair time under one failure definition, and list hazardous-failure measures that must be tracked separately from availability. Also recalculate availability for the alternative mtbf value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable; excluding reporting delays can also create an unrepresentative figure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。 逐項對照故障開始、服務恢復與維修完成時間，公開排除項，並核對總觀測時數。","textEn":"Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service. Cross-check fault start, service restoration and repair completion for each event, disclose exclusions, and verify total observed hours.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較提高故障間隔與縮短修復時間兩種措施，用同一故障定義重算，並列出可用度之外需要追蹤的危險失效指標。 再以本單元 mtbf 的對照值重算 availability，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare increasing failure interval with reducing repair time under one failure definition, and list hazardous-failure measures that must be tracked separately from availability. Also recalculate availability for the alternative mtbf value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「可用度與修復時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Availability and repair time\"?","options":["將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點"],"optionsEn":["Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b315-v16-40","title":"可用度與修復時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Availability and repair time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b315-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「可用度與修復時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Availability and repair time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。 修好設備和恢復服務可能不同時，須分別記錄終點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable; excluding reporting delays can also create an unrepresentative figure. Equipment repair and service restoration may occur at different times; record both endpoints. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把防水維修時間與正常設備修復分別納入停機紀錄。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Record waterproofing maintenance separately from normal equipment repair in downtime records.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b315-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。 修好設備和恢復服務可能不同時，須分別記錄終點。","textEn":"Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable; excluding reporting delays can also create an unrepresentative figure. Equipment repair and service restoration may occur at different times; record both endpoints.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]},{"id":"b315-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「可用度與修復時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Availability and repair time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable; excluding reporting delays can also create an unrepresentative figure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-b314-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b314-background"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b315-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b315-en.svg"}};
